    "description": "You’ll love this easy cookie recipe, perfect for cookie exchanges or just keeping folks happy during your holiday gatherings. Full of the flavors of the season and a pleasant tartness, they won’t last long! Begin by creaming butter with sugar and brown sugar, add an egg and mix in with orange zest and orange juice. Add flour, baking soda, salt and a combination of chopped fresh cranberries and walnuts. When they’re baked up fragrant, cool and drizzle with a delicious glaze of confectioners’ sugar, orange zest and orange juice. Dough freezes well, so make an extra batch for later!",
